Formula
$$ E_g=\frac{P\Phi ZN}{60A} $$

Where:

P = Number of poles
Φ = Flux per pole (Wb)
Z = Total armature conductors
N = Speed (RPM)
A = Parallel paths
# DC Generator EMF Calculator

P = int(input("Enter number of poles P: "))
phi = float(input("Enter flux per pole Φ (Wb): "))
Z = int(input("Enter total armature conductors Z: "))
N = float(input("Enter speed N (RPM): "))
A = int(input("Enter parallel paths A: "))

Eg = (P * phi * Z * N) / (60 * A)

print("Generated EMF =", Eg, "Volts")
Example

If:

P = 4
Φ = 0.02 Wb
Z = 500
N = 1000 RPM
A = 2

Generated EMF = 333.33 V
